  SELECT 'privacy', 'published', '1', $legal$## Who we are

Ecram Execs provides executive chauffeur services in the Netherlands and is the controller of the personal data described here. Questions about this policy can be sent to [enquiries@ecramexecs.com](mailto:enquiries@ecramexecs.com).

## What we collect and why

When you request a booking we collect your name, email address, phone number, the collection point, destination (or, for an hourly booking, how many hours), date and time of your journey and of any return journey, the service and number of passengers and suitcases you select, a flight number if you give one, the name and phone number of the person travelling if you book for someone else, and any notes you add. If you send a bespoke inquiry we also collect your company or account name, the size of your delegation, your vehicle class requirements, your itinerary and special instructions, and whether you prefer to be contacted by phone or WhatsApp. We use this only to arrange your booking or programme, arrange your journey and contact you about it. The legal basis is taking steps at your request before entering into a contract (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR).

When you apply to drive with us we collect your name, email address, phone number, KvK number, years of driving experience, your car's licence plate and any notes you add. We look the plate up in the public register of the RDW (the Dutch vehicle authority) to check the car against our criteria, and store the make, model, colour, seating, registration dates and taxi registration it returns. You also upload copies of your chauffeur card, KvK extract, certificate of conduct (VOG) and insurance; these are stored in a private storage area that only our team can open. We use this only to assess your application and, if it is approved, to work with you. The legal basis is taking steps at your request before entering into a contract (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR).

To protect the forms against abuse we also store a one-way, salted hash of your IP address and your browser's user-agent string. The hash cannot be turned back into your IP address. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in keeping the service secure (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).

If you use the chat concierge on the website, the messages you type are forwarded to our AI provider (see “Who processes your data”) so it can write a reply. We save the conversation for 90 days after its last message, or for one year if the chat led to a booking that we have confirmed. It includes what you tell the concierge about your journey and the name, email address and phone number you give it, together with a one-way hash of your IP address. We use it to refer back to what was agreed, to follow up on your request, to check the quality of the replies and to deal with misuse; it is deleted sooner if the booking request it led to is deleted. Please do not put sensitive personal data in the chat. If you choose to continue via WhatsApp, the conversation is passed on to WhatsApp Business at your request and WhatsApp's own privacy policy applies from that moment. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in answering your questions, following up on them and keeping the service secure (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR) and, where you ask for a quotation in the chat, taking steps at your request (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR). You can ask us to delete a conversation at any time.

A public booking can record how you heard about us (Google Search, a recommendation, social media, a corporate partner, or something you type in) and whether you agreed to news and offers. That marketing choice is consent under Article 6(1)(a) GDPR and you can withdraw it at any time. Close-protection bookings also store security notes. Those notes stay with the booking and only staff authorised for close protection can open them.

## Cookies {#cookies}

The public website does not set tracking, advertising, website-analytics, or Meta Pixel cookies unless you allow analytical or marketing cookies in the banner. Until you choose, analytics and the Meta Pixel stay off. A strictly necessary session cookie is used only when our staff sign in to the internal reservations system.

[[cookies]]

Our staff log in to an internal reservation system that uses its own session and language cookies; only staff receive these. The language choice also briefly stores your scroll position in your browser's session storage so the page stays where it was; no personal data is stored there and it disappears as soon as you close the tab.

## Who processes your data

We use carefully selected service providers who process data on our behalf under data processing agreements:

- GoDaddy (Host Europe GmbH) — hosting of the website, database and uploaded documents, on a server within the European Union
- Supabase — database and document storage, in the European Union
- Resend — delivery of email notifications about your request
- Anthropic — the AI that writes the chat concierge's replies; it receives the messages typed into the chat
- Moneybird — invoices and the billing details needed to send them
- Mollie — card and online payments, including the payment status we show on your booking
- WhatsApp Business (Meta) — messages you choose to send us on WhatsApp, handled under WhatsApp's own terms once the conversation moves there

When you type an address in the booking form, what you type is sent to Google to suggest matching places. Google receives only that text, not your name or contact details, and handles it under its own privacy policy; it may process it in the United States.

Resend and Anthropic are located in the United States. Where personal data is transferred outside the European Economic Area, we rely on the European Commission's standard contractual clauses in our agreements with them.

We do not sell your data or share it with third parties for marketing.

## How long we keep it

Booking and bespoke requests are kept for up to 24 months after our last contact with you, so we can handle follow-up questions and repeat bookings. Driver applications that do not lead to a partnership, including the documents uploaded with them, are kept for up to 12 months. Conversations with the chat concierge are kept for 90 days after the last message, or for one year if they led to a confirmed booking. Information that forms part of our financial records is kept for seven years, as Dutch tax law requires. You can ask us to delete your request at any time. Deleted data can remain in our backups for up to 14 days.

## Your rights

You have the right to access, correct or delete your personal data, to restrict or object to its processing, and to receive it in a portable format. Contact us at [enquiries@ecramexecs.com](mailto:enquiries@ecramexecs.com) and we will respond within one month. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Dutch Data Protection Authority ([Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens](https://autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl)).

## Security

Your data is transmitted over encrypted connections and stored in access-controlled systems. Only authorised staff can view booking and bespoke requests and driver applications. Security notes collected for close protection are restricted to staff who are authorised to handle that protection.

## Corporate partners

If you request access to our Corporate Partner area we collect your company email address, name and position, and the details you add to a corporate account request. We use your email address to send a one-time verification code (taking steps at your request, Article 6(1)(b) GDPR). If you tick the box on the form, we also use your details to keep you informed about our services and news by email, based on your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR); you can withdraw it at any time by contacting us, and we then stop. Verification codes expire after ten minutes and are stored only in a form that cannot be read back.

In this area you can request bookings, review bookings, send us messages and request a change or cancellation. We store the trip details you enter (collection point, destination or duration, stopovers, date and time, any return journey, number of passengers and suitcases, flight number, the person travelling if you book for someone else, vehicle and notes), your name, email address and phone number as booker, your company name and KvK number if you provided them, the price and status of the booking, and the messages and replies with it. If you submit the business introduction, we also store your company registration number, who signs on behalf of the company, a point of call, how you prefer to be contacted and which trips you expect to book. We use this to arrange your trips and reply to you (taking steps at your request and performance of our contract, Article 6(1)(b) GDPR). Our team can add invoices to a booking so you can download them; only you and our staff can open them.

If you tick the box when creating your account, we also use your details to keep you informed about our services and news by email, based on your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR). You can withdraw that consent at any time by contacting us.

We keep your account as long as you use it. If you have not logged in for 24 months and no work has been done on any of your bookings in that time, we delete it automatically, along with the bookings that are not part of our financial records. If you start creating an account without finishing it, we delete the details after 30 days. You can also ask us at any time to close your account and delete your data; we will do so, except for what we are legally required to keep: bookings that form part of our financial records, such as invoiced bookings, remain for seven years without your personal data (only the company, route, amount and invoices remain).$legal$, '2026-11-25', now(), now()
